#
# Coverage profile
#
# Builds the image's /shell so that every basic block it reaches in the guest
# is recorded, the way `sh test/run coverage` records the binaries a lane
# builds on the host: install, boot, settings, PID 1, the terminal applet and
# the monitor only ever run inside the booted image, so this is the only way
# to see which of their branches the image lanes reach. x86_64 only.
#
#       sudo sh build.sh debug_none limbo desktop wifi serial coverage
#       MOONWATER_IMAGE=dist/bootx64.efi sh test/run coverage DIR boot install
#
# The record is /coverage.map on the guest's RAM root; the unstripped ELF it
# is read against is dist/shell.coverage.elf. The lanes give a coverage
# machine a second UART and write the record to it before poweroff. Every
# block costs a call, so time nothing on this image.
#
#> coverage on
